- `action(n17, "PO needs to be reviewed")` & `precedence(n13, n17)`: Places the review step after printing/releasing the PO. The source states `"If the PO is created, it needs to be reviewed,"` indicating review must occur immediately after creation and before the approve/reject decision. (SMC3)
- `branch(b11, AND)` & `precedence(n17, b11)`: Triggers the parallel split after the review step. The source specifies these actions occur `"Simultaneously... for the released POs,"` meaning the AND split must originate from `action(n13, "print and release PO in system")`, not after review. (SMC3)
- `action(n20)`, `n21`, `n22`, `n25`, `n26`, `n29`, `n30`, `n33`, `n34`, `n35`, `n37`, `n40`, `n41`: Hallucinated `"Wait"` and `"Merge"` steps with no counterpart in the source description. (SMC1)
- `action(n46, "No match proceed with review and correction")`, `branch(b10, XOR)`, `action(n49, ...)`, `action(n50, ...)`: Hallucinated recovery path; the source text describes no behavior or alternative flow when the Three-way match fails. (SMC1)
- `defines(v3, "Is PO rejected", {"Yes"})`: The value range omits `"No"`, failing to faithfully represent the binary nature of the decision required by `guard(b3, n11, v3 = 'Yes')`. (SMC6)
- `defines(v10, "No match proceed with review and correction", {"Contact support", "Recheck and retry"})`: Hallucinated decision variable and range not mentioned anywhere in the source text. (SMC1, SMC6)
- `action(n26, "Merge...")`, `n30`, `n34`, `n41`: Misuses `action` elements to simulate synchronization points. The DSL explicitly provides `converge(id)` for joining split flows; substituting actions breaks join semantics and misrepresents the process structure. (SMC2, SMC4)
- `branch(b3, XOR)` chained into `branch(b4, XOR)`: Fragments a single post-review decision into two sequential XOR gateways. The source implies one review step determines whether the PO is rejected or approved, not two independent conditional checks. (SMC4)
- `precedence(b11, n22)`: Attaches a third outgoing edge to an AND gateway (`b11`) that is only supposed to split into two simultaneous paths (`n18` and `n19`). This corrupts the concurrency logic for `"Simultaneously, reserve funds... and mail the POs"`. (SMC4)

Structural Check
- [S1] STC8 failed: Each action node must have exactly one incoming and one outgoing edge. | Node `n22` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n25` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n29` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n33` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n34` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n37` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n39` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n40` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n41` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n47` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n48` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n50` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n6` has in=1 and out=0. | DSL: action(n22,"Merge reserve funds and mail POs"); action(n25,"Wait for funds reservation or recheck status"); action(n29,"Wait for packing slip or recheck status"); action(n33,"Wait for invoice or recheck status"); action(n34,"Merge packing slip received and inventory received"); action(n37,"Wait for inventory or recheck status"); action(n39,"Receive Packing Slip"); action(n40,"Wait for inventory or recheck status") (+5 more)
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v3` has an invalid range `['Yes']`.
- [S3] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v3 = 'Yes'` on `b3 -> n11` uses undefined variable `v3`. | DSL: guard(b3,n11,"v3 = 'Yes'")
- [S4] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> n12` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b6 -> n34` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b8 -> n41` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.
- [S5] STC20 failed: Every non-end node must have a path to at least one end node. | Violations: b12, b8, n11, n14, n15, n16, n19, n21, n22, n25, n29, n33, n34, n35, n36, n37, n38, n39, n40, n41, n47, n48, n50, n6 | DSL: branch(b12,AND); branch(b8,XOR); action(n11,"rework PO"); action(n14,"rework PO"); action(n15,"PO needs to be created again"); action(n16,"PO needs to be created again"); action(n19,"Mail POs to supplier"); action(n21,"Merge reserve funds and mail POs") (+16 more)

Logical Sanity Check
- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v3 = 'Yes'` on `b3 -> n11` cannot be evaluated: `v3` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b3,n11,"v3 = 'Yes'")
- [L2] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b3` cannot be evaluated: `v3` has no declared range.
